// The Seven Bridges (bible 4.4, 8.4). Halvard's second hunt on the last span (Bridges_4; boss 6.3, second kit).
// And the Seventh Bridge (Bridges_3): "under repair" for forty years; the Arden family is paid to stand on it.
// And the Master's Exam (Hall_3): Tam's eleven identical years of notes (plant 5.1).

title: Bridges_Halvard_Hunt
---
<<if has_flag("boss.halvard_2.defeated")>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Halvard: Journeyman. Four paces, now. I said I'd measured you.
Halvard: The bridge is Guild property. So is the fall. I've a new lance for it.
-> Still counting, Sergeant?
    Halvard: Always. Twice now. There is no third book.
    <<voice surveyor halden>>
-> Stand aside. I'm going to the Hall.
    Halvard: Through me, then. The Hall can wait on the count.
    <<voice warden halden>>
-> ...
    Halvard: Entered as a plea. Again. You've a talent for it.
    <<voice drift halden>>
<<flag act2.halvard_second 1>>
===

title: Bridges_Family
---
<<if has_flag("halden.bridge.family_met")>>
    Arden: Under repair. We are the repair. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Arden: Under repair. Keep to the left.
Arden: We are paid to stand here. My grandmother stood here, and her son. Now us.
Arden: The Bridge Office says the stone is weak. If we step off, it might fall. Nobody has tested it.
-> Has anyone looked at the stone?
    Arden: Looked? It's under repair. You don't look at a thing under repair. You wait.
-> Step off. I'll catch you if it goes.
    Arden: And lose the wage? Forty years of wage? No. Thank you. Kindly meant.
-> ...
    Arden: Aye. It's peaceful, standing. You'd be surprised.
<<flag halden.bridge.family_met 1>>
===

title: Hall_Tam
---
<<if has_flag("halden.exam.notes_read")>>
    Tam: Next spring. I feel good about next spring. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Tam: Wren! You're back. Are you sitting it? Next spring. I'm sitting it next spring.
Tam: I've got my notes. Eleven books. I start a fresh one each year, to be safe.
Tam: Look. The same, see? Every year I get it right. I just need to sit it. #plant:5.1
-> These are identical, Tam. Every page.
    Tam: Well, the answers don't change. That's what makes them answers.
-> When did you start revising?
    Tam: Last autumn. Just last autumn. Time goes quickly in the Hall.
-> ...
    Tam: You look tired. Revising? Me too. Always.
<<flag halden.exam.notes_read 1>>
===
